   "project": "ledgerlite",
   "reply": "The command that works, run from the project root, is:\n\n```\nPYTHONPATH=src python -m unittest discover -s tests -v\n```\n\nIt ran 2 tests and both passed.\n\n- **Why unittest:** The tests are written with `unittest`, and `pytest` isn't installed. `python -m pytest tests` fails with \"No module named pytest\".\n- **Why `PYTHONPATH=src`:** The package lives in `src/ledgerlite`, and the project has no install step. Without `PYTHONPATH=src`, the `from ledgerlite import Ledger` import in the tests will likely fail. I didn't run it without that setting to confirm.\n- **Shell:** The command is for Git Bash. In PowerShell, set the variable separately with `$env:PYTHONPATH=\"src\"`.",
